  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><strong>Aura</strong> faint (+1), moderate (+2/+3), or strong (+4/+5) Alteration and Enhancement; <strong>CL</strong> 5th (+1), 6th (+2), 9th (+3), 12th (+4), or 15th (+5)<br>\n<strong>Slot</strong> neck; <strong>Price</strong> 6,000 gp (+1), 24,000 gp (+2), 54,000 gp (+3), 96,000 gp (+4), or 150,000 gp (+5); <strong>Weight</strong> 1&nbsp;lb.</p>\n<p>A much-beloved item among the wealthy and talented brawlers of the world, a pugilist’s charm grants a +1 to +5 enhancement bonus to attack and damage rolls with unarmed strikes and natural weapons, and an equal enhancement bonus to the wearer’s natural armor.</p>\n<p><strong>Author's Note:</strong> You may apply weapon special abilities to your unarmed strikes instead of bonuses to attack and damage rolls, at the same price.</p>\n<p><strong>Construction Requirements</strong><br>\nForge Charm, Alteration sphere, Enhancement sphere; <strong>Cost</strong> 3,000 gp (+1), 12,000 gp (+2), 27,000 gp (+3), 48,000 gp (+4), or 75,000 gp (+5)</p>\n<p><a href=\"http://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/charms#toc34\">Source: Spheres of Power Wiki</a></p>",
      "instructions": "<p>Reviewed selection: base +1 enhancement, 6000 gp; no weapon special abilities selected.</p><p>The selected +1 grants enhancement to natural-weapon attack/damage and to natural armor. Unarmed strikes also qualify in the rules, but PF1's core Unarmed Strike has weapon subtype while nattack/ndamage cover natural subtype only. Its unarmed bonus remains an explicit manual step under issue #38; do not apply a global weapon bonus. The alternative weapon-property option is unselected and would replace the relevant attack/damage bonus as stated, not add free properties.</p>",
      "unidentified": ""
    },
